/* Huffman coding — the fire-bringer's compression.

   Counts character frequencies, merges the two cheapest nodes until one
   tree remains, walks it assigning bit codes (left = 0, right = 1), packs
   the whole message into a single bits value, and decodes it back to prove
   the round trip.

   Codes are stored as (pattern, width) pairs: a bits value carries its own
   width for display, but nothing in the language will tell you that width
   as a number, and the packer needs it. */

Define object hnode with (the text symbol, the number freq, the series of hnode children).
Define object hcode with (the bits pattern, the number width).

Bind map from text to number to frequencies, given (the text source):
    Define counts as a map from text to number.
    Define total as the length of source.
    Define i as 1.
    While i is not greater than total, repeat:
        Define ch as the characters from i to i of source.
        If counts has a key for ch:
            Define old as the entry for ch in counts but void is 0.
            In counts, the entry for ch becomes old + 1.
        Done.
        Otherwise, in counts, the entry for ch becomes 1.
        The i becomes i + 1.
    Done.
    Return counts.
Done.

Bind series of hnode to leaves-from, given (the map from text to number counts):
    Define leaves as a series of hnode.
    For each pair in counts, repeat:
        Define sym as the key of pair.
        Define n as the value of pair.
        Add a new hnode { the symbol sym, the freq n, the children a series of hnode } to leaves.
    Done.
    Return leaves.
Done.

Bind hnode to build-tree, given (the series of hnode leaves):
    Define queue as leaves sorted by the freq.
    Define count as the number of queue.
    While count is greater than 1, repeat:
        Define least as the first of queue.
        Define next-least as item 2 of queue.
        Remove the first item from queue.
        Remove the first item from queue.
        Define merged as a new hnode { the symbol "", the freq least's freq + next-least's freq,
                                       the children a series of hnode with (least, next-least) }.
        Add merged to queue.
        The queue becomes queue sorted by the freq.
        The count becomes the number of queue.
    Done.
    Return the first of queue.
Done.

/* Left appends a 0 bit, right appends a 1. At the root (w is 0) the codes
   are simply 0b0 and 0b1, so depth-one codes are exactly one digit. */
Bind void to assign-codes, given (the hnode node, the bits pat, the number w,
                                  the map from text to hcode codes):
    If the number of node's children is 0:
        In codes, the entry for node's symbol becomes a new hcode { the pattern pat, the width w }.
        Return.
    Done.
    Define left-kid as the first of node's children.
    Define right-kid as item 2 of node's children.
    Define left-pat as 0b0.
    Define right-pat as 0b1.
    Define next-w as 1.
    If w is greater than 0:
        The left-pat becomes pat shifted left by 1.
        The right-pat becomes (pat shifted left by 1) or 0b1.
        The next-w becomes w + 1.
    Done.
    Cast assign-codes on (left-kid, left-pat, next-w, codes).
    Cast assign-codes on (right-kid, right-pat, next-w, codes).
Done.

/* Pack codes into a series of bits-values, never letting one value pass
   the 64-bit ceiling. A code that would straddle a boundary closes the
   current chunk and starts the next, so every chunk's printed digits are
   exactly its bits and decode is a plain walk over chunks. */
Bind series of hcode to encode, given (the text source, the map from text to hcode codes):
    Define chunks as a series of hcode.
    Define acc as 0b0.
    Define fill as 0.
    Define started as false.
    Define total as the length of source.
    Define i as 1.
    While i is not greater than total, repeat:
        Define ch as the characters from i to i of source.
        Define code as the entry for ch in codes.
        If code is not void:
            Define w as code's width.
            Define pat as code's pattern.
            If started is false:
                The acc becomes pat.
                The fill becomes w.
                The started becomes true.
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                Define need as fill + w.
                If need is greater than 64:
                    Add a new hcode { the pattern acc, the width fill } to chunks.
                    The acc becomes pat.
                    The fill becomes w.
                Done.
                Otherwise:
                    The acc becomes (acc shifted left by w) or pat.
                    The fill becomes fill + w.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        The i becomes i + 1.
    Done.
    If started is true, add a new hcode { the pattern acc, the width fill } to chunks.
    Return chunks.
Done.

/* Walk each chunk from its top bit; a leaf emits its symbol. Chunks are
   self-describing via their stored width, so no position arithmetic. */
Bind text to decode, given (the series of hcode chunks, the hnode root):
    Define out as "".
    Define node as root.
    For each chunk in chunks, repeat:
        Define pattern as chunk's pattern.
        Define width as chunk's width.
        Define pos as 1.
        While pos is not greater than width, repeat:
            Define drop as width - pos.
            Define aligned as pattern shifted right by drop.
            Define bit as (aligned and 0b1) converted to number.
            Define kids as node's children.
            If bit is 0, the node becomes the first of kids.
            Otherwise, the node becomes item 2 of kids.
            If the number of node's children is 0:
                The out becomes out joined to node's symbol.
                The node becomes root.
            Done.
            The pos becomes pos + 1.
        Done.
    Done.
    Return out.
Done.

Bind void to play:
    Define message as "the rabbit brings fire to the people".

    Define counts as cast frequencies on (message).
    Define leaves as cast leaves-from on (counts).
    Define root as cast build-tree on (leaves).
    Define codes as a map from text to hcode.
    If the number of root's children is 0, in codes, the entry for root's symbol becomes a new hcode 
                                                   { the pattern 0b1, the width 1 }.
    Otherwise, cast assign-codes on (root, 0b0, 0, codes).

    State "message: {message}".
    State "".
    State "code table:".
    For each pair in codes, repeat:
        Define sym as the key of pair.
        Define code as the value of pair.
        Define pat-text as code's pattern converted to text.
        Define w-text as code's width converted to text.
        State "  {sym} -> {pat-text} ({w-text} bits)".
    Done.

    Define packed as cast encode on (message, codes).
    Define chunk-count as the number of packed.
    Define total-bits as 0.
    State "".
    State "encoded in {chunk-count converted to text} chunks:".
    For each chunk in packed, repeat:
        Define pat-text as chunk's pattern converted to text.
        Define w-text as chunk's width converted to text.
        Define w as chunk's width.
        The total-bits becomes total-bits + w.
        State "  {pat-text} ({w-text} bits)".
    Done.
    Define chars as the length of message.
    Define raw-bits as chars * 8.
    State "packed to {total-bits converted to text} bits, versus {raw-bits converted to text} at a byte per character".

    Define round-trip as cast decode on (packed, root).
    State "".
    If round-trip is message:
        State "decoded: {round-trip}".
        State "round trip holds".
    Done.
    Otherwise, state "MISMATCH: {round-trip}".
Done.

Cast play.